{"availability":"available","full":"lago-morph/software-factory","name":"software-factory","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-10T20:02:40Z","updated":"2026-06-08T00:46:36Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":null,"color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A primer on what this repository is exploring: how to get serious leverage from a skilled engineer's attention by coupling AI inference with the right tools and discipline. This document is for someone curious about the work but new to it. It's a point-in-time snapshot as of May 2026 — the conclusions will change as the experiments run, and parts of this will read as dated in a few months.","We did not start with one answer. The exploration in this repository takes seriously that there are several plausible shapes for what a \"software factory\" looks like — they're not the same, they involve different tradeoffs, and they probably suit different kinds of work. So the work converged on ten candidate methodologies, each with a specific bet about what the load-bearing piece is. The candidates aren't all compatible. Some are direct competitors; some address different mandates (more on that below). The point of having ten is to be able to compare them apples-to-apples and to design…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lago-morph/software-factory/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"053c5a76b89b2d10a1ba34500c34615931f5b9fb74060cac9e6b6f601006a016","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:49:52.155Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A primer on what this repository is exploring: how to get serious leverage from a skilled engineer's attention by coupling AI inference with the right tools and discipline. This document is for someone curious about the work but new to it. It's a point-in-time snapshot as of May 2026 — the conclusions will change as the experiments run, and parts of this will read as dated in a few months.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lago-morph/software-factory/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"Most current AI-on-brownfield setups have the agent read source files into its context window every time it needs to understand something, paying the comprehension cost over and over.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lago-morph/software-factory/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"At high parallelism, the FC graph could get expensive — every artifact needs an opposing-side call, and at scale the cost could dominate.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lago-morph/software-factory/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"053c5a76b89b2d10a1ba34500c34615931f5b9fb74060cac9e6b6f601006a016","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lago-morph/software-factory/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T05:49:52.155Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-06-08T00:46:36Z","overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T05:49:42.854Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lago-morph/software-factory/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T05:49:52.158Z","hash":"053c5a76b89b2d10a1ba34500c34615931f5b9fb74060cac9e6b6f601006a016","originalBytes":56967,"storedBytes":56967,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["what","work","they","model","agent","every","substrate","code","how","makes","methodology","spec","candidates","intent","system","different","each","brownfield","codebase","greenfield","most","when","candidate","could","load-bearing","one","architecture","build","where","actually","arti